# BetConstruct is iframe-first

BetConstruct integration uses BetConstruct-hosted iFrames. Do not invent a parallel Nextpari sportsbook or casino client for this provider.

## Do not build

- a Nextpari BetConstruct event feed
- Nextpari BetConstruct markets UI
- a Nextpari BetConstruct betslip
- Nextpari BetConstruct casino/game UI
- BetConstruct market ingestion into `sportsStore`
- synchronization of BetConstruct markets into the native sportsbook UI
- routing BetConstruct bets through the native Nextpari sports engine (`sports_engine_place`, LSports quotes, native betslip)

Native LSports sportsbook remains separate and unchanged.

## BetConstruct owns inside the iframe

Sportsbook UI, prematch, live, markets, betslip, bet acceptance/trading UI, and casino/game UI.

## Nextpari owns

- player authentication
- opaque short-lived AuthToken plus separate launch-session metadata
- active wallet and currency
- player balance
- Wallet Ledger (all actual player-money changes)
- method-specific provider callback endpoints
- security restrictions
- deposits/withdrawals outside the provider iframe
- provider accounting/reconciliation

## Sportsbook flow

Nextpari frontend requests a launch session from Nextpari backend → receives `iframeUrl`, `providerOrigin`, currency, product, and a short-lived opaque AuthToken → opens the BetConstruct iframe only if the iframe URL origin matches `providerOrigin`, with `integrationMode=1` and `AuthToken`. BetConstruct then calls Nextpari Operator API at method-specific URLs:

- `POST /api/betconstruct/operator/GetClientDetails`
- `POST /api/betconstruct/operator/GetClientBalance`
- `POST /api/betconstruct/operator/BetPlaced`
- `POST /api/betconstruct/operator/BetResulted`
- `POST /api/betconstruct/operator/Rollback`

Do not require a JSON `method` field for routing.

## Casino flow

Nextpari frontend requests a casino game launch → opens the provider-hosted game iframe after the same origin check. BetConstruct RGS calls Nextpari Single Wallet at method-specific URLs:

- `POST /api/betconstruct/wallet/Authentication`
- `POST /api/betconstruct/wallet/GetBalance`
- `POST /api/betconstruct/wallet/Withdraw`
- `POST /api/betconstruct/wallet/Deposit`
- `POST /api/betconstruct/wallet/WithdrawAndDeposit`
- `POST /api/betconstruct/wallet/Rollback`

## Credentials

Sportsbook and Casino credentials are separate. Do not assume one SharedKey or one IP allowlist covers both:

- `BETCONSTRUCT_SPORTS_SHARED_KEY`
- `BETCONSTRUCT_SPORTS_ALLOWED_IPS`
- `BETCONSTRUCT_CASINO_SHARED_KEY`
- `BETCONSTRUCT_CASINO_ALLOWED_IPS`
- `BETCONSTRUCT_OPERATOR_ID`
- `BETCONSTRUCT_SPORTSBOOK_IFRAME_ORIGIN`
- `BETCONSTRUCT_CASINO_IFRAME_ORIGIN`
- `BETCONSTRUCT_ENABLED` (future master switch only)

No `VITE_*` provider secrets.

## Enablement

Keep the integration fail-closed until real test credentials, domain, SharedKeys, OperatorId, and IP allowlists are supplied. Do not treat dummy env as production-ready. Do not move player money until Wallet Ledger adapters are explicitly wired in a later phase.
